docs {
  # care-abdm-sbx — plug API collection

  This collection calls the ABDM plug routes on Care. It does not call ABDM directly.
  The plug does the encryption, the gateway session, and the token storage on the server.

  Source of truth: `backend/src/abdm/urls.py`. The MFE mirror is `frontend/src/lib/careApi.ts`.

  ## Before you start

  1. Run Care with the plug installed. See `docs/04-dev-setup.md`.
  2. Select the `local` environment.
  3. Set the secret variables `careUsername` and `carePassword` in the environment.
  4. Send `auth > 1. Login`. The script saves `careToken` to the environment.

  ## Variables

  | Variable | Job |
  |---|---|
  | `careUrl` | Base URL of Care. Default `http://localhost:8000` |
  | `careToken` | Care JWT access token. The login request saves it |
  | `careRefreshToken` | Care JWT refresh token. The login request saves it |
  | `facilityId` | `external_id` of the Care facility |
  | `patientId` | `external_id` of the Care patient |
  | `txnId` | ABDM transaction id. The OTP requests save it |
  | `callbackId` | `id` of a stored callback. The callback list saves it |
  | `hipId` | HIP identifier that the gateway sends as `X-HIP-ID` |
  | `callbackToken` | Signed JWT that the gateway sends in the callback `Authorization` header |
  | `linkRefNumber` | Link reference number from the link init step |
  | `encounterId` | `external_id` of the Care encounter (= care context reference) |
  | `shareItemId` | `id` of a share item from the care-context GET |
  | `consentId` | Consent artefact id from a consent notification |
  | `hiuPublicKey`, `hiuNonce` | Base64 X25519 public key and 32-byte nonce of a test HIU |
  | `consentRequestRowId` | `id` of a consent request row (hiu > 1 and 2 save it) |
  | `consentRequestId` | The HIE-CM consent request id, from the `on-init` callback |
  | `outboundRequestId` | REQUEST-ID of the plug call a callback answers (`response.requestId`) |
  | `otherHipId` | Service id of the facility that holds the records (the HIP in an artefact) |
  | `transactionId` | Health-information transaction id, from the `on-request` callback |
  | `fetchedRecordId` | `id` of a fetched record (hiu > 1 saves the newest) |
  | `encryptedContent`, `contentChecksum`, `hipPublicKey`, `hipNonce` | A HIP-side encrypted entry for the data push probe |
  | `hfrFacilityId` | An `IN` facility id to look up or link (nhpr folder) |
  | `hprId`, `hprPassword` (secret), `hprLoginId` | The caller's HPR ID, its password, and a pending OTP login id |

  The pre-request script of this collection sets 2 more variables for each request:
  `requestId` is a new UUID, and `timestamp` is the time now in UTC with milliseconds.
  The callback requests send them as `REQUEST-ID` and `TIMESTAMP`.

  Secret variables hold the credentials and the personal data: `careUsername`,
  `carePassword`, `aadhaarNumber`, `mobileNumber`, `otp`. Bruno keeps these values
  out of the file.

  ## Rules

  - Each request sends the token in an explicit `Authorization` header.
  - The callback requests send the gateway signature token, not the Care token.
  - The plug relays an ABDM failure as HTTP 502 with `abdm_code`, `message`, and `request_id`.
}

script:pre-request {
  // The gateway sends a fresh REQUEST-ID and a UTC TIMESTAMP with each callback.
  // The callback requests read these 2 runtime variables.
  bru.setVar(
    "requestId",
    "xxxxxxxx-xxxx-4xxx-yxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx".replace(/[xy]/g, (c) => {
      const r = (Math.random() * 16) | 0;
      const v = c === "x" ? r : (r & 0x3) | 0x8;
      return v.toString(16);
    })
  );
  bru.setVar("timestamp", new Date().toISOString());
}
